<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haute-Loire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haute-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massif-central">Massif Central</a> in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, in the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region, with its prefecture at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-puy-en-velay">Le Puy-en-Velay</a>. Created in 1790, it covers the upper valley of the Loire and most of the old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velay">Velay</a>, with parts of Auvergne and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gevaudan">Gévaudan</a>. It is a land of volcanic plateaux, pasture and forest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haute-loire.jpg" alt="Haute-Loire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: KlausFoehl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mont_M%C3%A9zenc03_2016-05-20.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
